{%- comment -%}
  A single block of prose that answers one question properly.

  Two jobs on this site, and both come straight out of what the good hardware
  pages do:

  1. **Promote the objection to a heading.** Arccos runs sections literally
     titled "DO I NEED SENSORS ON MY CLUBS?" — the thing the buyer is already
     thinking, set as the headline, answered in plain words. Ours is "the app
     is free, so what am I paying for?", and burying that in an FAQ treats it
     as an edge case when it is the whole decision.

  2. **A founder note.** With no reviews, no press and no rating widget, the
     substitute for social proof is a person putting their name to it. Playdate
     ("The Idea", "Who Made It?") and Bellroy ("From the designer") both do
     this; for a one-person company it is the cheapest credibility available
     and the only kind that is entirely true.

  Deliberately no icons and no three-up grid — an icon row makes a physical
  product look like software.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section class="stmt full-width{% if section.settings.tone == 'dark' %} stmt--dark{% endif %}">
  <div class="stmt-inner">
    {%- if section.settings.label != blank -%}
      <p class="stmt-label">{{ section.settings.label }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <h2 class="stmt-title">{{ section.settings.title }}</h2>

    <div class="stmt-body">{{ section.settings.body }}</div>

    {%- if section.settings.signature != blank -%}
      <p class="stmt-signature">{{ section.settings.signature }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
  .stmt {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--content-grid);
    background: var(--bg);
    padding-block: clamp(72px, 10vw, 120px);
  }

  .stmt--dark { background: var(--bg2); }

  /* Left aligned and measure-limited. Centred body copy is the sales-page
     tell, and this section's whole job is to not sound like a sales page. */
  .stmt-inner {
    grid-column: 2;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .stmt-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--green);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .stmt-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--white);
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .stmt-body {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .stmt-body p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .stmt-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .stmt-body strong { color: var(--white); font-weight: 500; }
  .stmt-body a { color: var(--green); }

  .stmt-signature {
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--green);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Statement",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Eyebrow" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Heading", "default": "Heading" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "Body",
      "default": "<p>Body copy.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "signature", "label": "Signature", "info": "Optional. Use for a founder note." },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "tone",
      "label": "Background",
      "options": [
        { "value": "light", "label": "Base" },
        { "value": "dark", "label": "Raised" }
      ],
      "default": "light"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Statement" }]
}
{% endschema %}
